== bold: the corner house after the dark / R
base: go round tonight with a hot dinner and say sorry for that week
likelier_if: mark 'owned up' +10; mark 'helped someone in need' +5
- R | ask him to his face to forgive you, and sit with him every evening this winter | v: benevolence, stimulation | act: ask him to forgive them, and sit with him every evening that winter | chance: 30 | requires: good name in town | grants: friend for life | takes_if_fails: good name in town
works: He makes {N} wait on the step for a long minute, then lets {N} in, and by spring the two of them are friends for life.
works: The evenings turn into stories and card games, and the old man and {N} stay close for good.
fails: He shuts the door in front of half the street, the story goes round, and {Ns} good name on the street goes with it.
fails: {N} gives up after a week of closed doors, and the street decides {N} only cared about looking good.

# ================================================================ the town builds itself back

== bold: the town builds itself back / U
base: learn a building trade on the council's rebuilding course
likelier_if: has [public speaking] +10; has [bookkeeping] +10; has [good name in town] +5
- U | stand up at the town meeting and show, figure by figure, where the money runs out | v: universalism, self-direction | act: stand up at the town meeting and show, figure by figure, where the money runs out | chance: 45 | grants: voice at the town hall | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The council checks {Ns} sums, finds them right, and moves the clinic up the list; from then on {N} has a voice at the town hall.
works: The figures are in the paper by Friday, and the council starts asking {N} before it decides anything.
fails: The meeting turns on {N} for slowing the rebuilding down, and {N} is pushed off the residents' group.
fails: The figures are waved away, and {N} walks out of the residents' group in disgust and does not go back.

== bold: the town builds itself back / B
base: bid for a small rebuilding contract while the money is flowing
likelier_if: has [building trade] +10; has [contact in the trade] +10; has [striking a deal] +5
- B | stake your savings on a bid for the school's whole rebuilding contract | v: achievement, power | act: stake their savings on a bid for the school's whole rebuilding contract | chance: 30 | requires: savings | title: founder of a firm | takes_if_fails: savings
works: {N} wins the school contract, sets up a firm to do it, and the children are back in their own building within the year.
works: The bid comes in lowest and soundest, and by spring {N} has a firm of {Ns} own with the school as its first job.
fails: The contract goes to a bigger firm from out of town, and the savings spent on the bid are gone.
fails: The bid is thrown out on a detail, and the savings that went into it cannot be got back.

